{{Quote|This is Kalevala. It's another planet in the Mandalorian system. And that is a Mandalorian castle.|Din Djarin|audio=KryzeCastleIntro.flac|<ref name="Apostate" /> }}
'''Kryze Fortress''', also known as '''Kryze Castle''', was a [[Mandalorian]] castle located atop a [[Plant|lush]] hill by the [[Water|seaside]] on the [[planet]] [[Kalevala]]. It was the ancestral home and dwelling place of [[House Kryze]]. The castle featured a landing platform, including a large courtyard at the back of the castle for landing purposes. The castle itself consisted of a [[throne]] room containing various murals of Mandalorians in battle.

During the [[New Republic Era]], the castle was the home of [[Lady]] [[Bo-Katan Kryze]], where she was visited by Mandalorian [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] and the [[Force-sensitive]] [[foundling]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] in Djarin's [[Mission to the Living Waters|quest]] to be redeemed by bathing in the [[Living Waters]]. 

After Djarin successfully bathed in the waters, Kryze, Djarin, Grogu, and the [[R5 series astromech droid]] [[R5-D4]] went back to the castle where they were pursued by [[TIE/IN interceptor]]s, all from [[Gideon's Imperial remnant]]. The group managed to destroy all six [[interceptor]]s; however, by then, three [[TIE/sa tactical bomber|TIE/sa bombers]] from the same remnant arrived and [[Bomber|bombed]] the castle, destroying it.

==Description==
[[File:Kryze_Castle_throne_room.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The throne room of Kryze Castle]]
Kryze Fortress<ref name="CGttSWG">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref>, also known as Kryze Castle,<ref name="Audio Description">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> was located atop a [[Plant|lush]] hill by the [[Water|seaside]] on the terrestial [[planet]] [[Kalevala]]. The castle was affiliated to the [[Mandalorian]] [[House Kryze]],<ref name="Apostate" /> a [[Mandalorian house]] that served as the royal family of the Mandalorians before the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="The Mines of Mandalore">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore}}</ref> a [[The galaxy|galaxy]]-spanning conflict between the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref>  and it served as the personal residence of [[Lady]] [[Bo-Katan Kryze]]<ref name="Apostate" /> by [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Mando S3 Date" /> It had a small, heptagon-shaped landing platform<ref name="Apostate" /> and a large courtyard at the back of the castle<ref name="The Convert">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 19: The Convert}}</ref> that by the [[New Republic Era]] housed a [[Kom'rk-class fighter/transport|''Kom'rk''-class fighter]] which served as the personal [[transport]] for Kryze.<ref name="The Mines of Mandalore" /> 

Those visiting the castle would be greeted by a large main tower containing the [[throne]] room which was adorned with the banners of House Kryze along its hallways. The throne room consisted of a throne next to two small vases and two large vases.<ref name="Apostate" /> Two<ref name="The Mines of Mandalore" /> murals were also beside the throne depicting Mandalorians in battle. By the [[New Republic]] Era, a [[Bo-Katan Kryze's footman droid|footman droid]] with the symbol of the [[Ka'rta]] embedded into its chest was present at the landing platform to supervise and monitor any arriving [[Starship|ships]].<ref name="Apostate" />

==History==
{{Quote|Those mudscuffers bombed my home!|Kryze|audio=Kryze Castle-AudioFile.flac|<ref name="The Convert" />}}
[[File:BoKatanChapter17.png|thumb|left|300px|Bo-Katan Kryze decided to stay in Kryze Castle after she was unable to obtain the Darksaber.]]
Kryze Fortress was the ancestral home and dwelling place of the House of Kryze.<ref name="CGttSWG" /> In the [[Republic Era]], during Kryze's childhood, Kryze grew up flying the various cliffs near the castle.<ref name="The Convert" /> By 9 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> in the time of the [[New Republic Era]], Kryze along with her [[Bo-Katan Kryze's unit|followers]] made an [[Search for the Darksaber|effort]] to reclaim the [[Darksaber]],<ref name="The Heiress">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> a symbolic [[lightsaber]] crafted by the first Mandalorian [[Jedi]] [[Tarre Vizsla]] which could reunite the Mandalorians,<ref name="Return">{{BOBF|Chapter 5: Return of the Mandalorian}}</ref> from [[Moff]] [[Gideon]], an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[warlord]] who led a [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|remnant]].<ref name="The Heiress" /> In 9 ABY,<ref name="Timelines" /> Kryze as well as her followers were recruited by the Mandalorian [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] to [[Second rescue of Grogu|rescue]] the [[Force-sensitive]] [[foundling]] [[Din Grogu|Grogu]] from Gideon's remnant. In exchange, Kryze could claim Gideon's [[Gideon's light cruiser|light cruiser]] and the Darksaber. During the rescue, Djarin managed to defeat Gideon leading to Kryze being unable to obtain the Darksaber as it could only be obtained by combat.<ref name="The Rescue">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref> Following the rescue, the [[Mandalorian fleet|forces]] that she amassed to [[Conflict on Mandalore|retake]] [[Mandalore]], a planet located in the same [[Mandalore system|system]] as Kalevala, melted away leading her to stay at the castle with her [[footman droid]].<ref name="Apostate" />

Around that [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="Mando S3 Date" /> Djarin as well as Grogu visited the castle, where they met with Kryze. Djarin asked Kryze if he could join her forces to which Kryze responded that there was nothing to join. After Kryze and Djarin discussed Kryze's previous army plus the Darksaber, Djarin stated to Kryze that he was going to the Mines of Mandalore to atone for his transgressions in the eyes of the [[Children of the Watch]],<ref name="Apostate" /> an orthodox [[Religion|religious]] faction of Mandalorians that followed the [[Way of the Mandalore]].<ref name="Return" /> Djarin also stated that he would atone by bathing in the [[Living Waters]],<ref name="Apostate" /> a ceremonial ground located in the Mines of Mandalore which, according to [[Mandalorian Creed]], could redeem a Mandalorian [[Apostate (religion)|apostate]] who took of their [[helmet]].<ref name="Return" /> Kryze told Djarin about the mines and how there was nothing special about them, prompting Djarin to state how Kryze said that the curse on Mandalore was a lie. Kryze then told Djarin where the mines were leading to Djarin and Grogu to leave the castle to go to the mines.<ref name="Apostate" />

Grogu along with the [[R5 series astromech droid]] [[R5-D4]] later returned to the castle in [[Din Djarin's N-1 starfighter|Djarin's N-1 starfighter]] to seek the help of Kryze in saving Djarin, who was captured by a [[Cyborg mech|cyborg]] [[scavenger]] on Mandalore in an attempt to take his [[blood]]. After Kryze had misunderstood that Djarin had returned to the castle and realized that Djarin was in trouble, she immediately proceeded to her [[Bo-Katan Kryze's Gauntlet starfighter|''Kom'rk''-class fighter]] parked at the castle. She left the castle in her [[starfighter]] with Grogu and R5-D4 to go to Mandalore and save Djarin.<ref name="The Mines of Mandalore" />

[[File:KryzeCastleDestroyed-TMch19.png|thumb|right|300px|Kryze Castle was destroyed by forces from the Imperial remnant.]]
Kryze managed to save Djarin who later bathed in the Living Waters. Kryze, Djarin, R5-D4, plus Grogu then left Mandalore to return to Kalevala. While en route in Kryze's fighter, they were pursued by at least six [[TIE/IN interceptor]]s, all from Gideon's Imperial remnant, and engaged in a [[Bombing of Kryze Castle|dogfight]] near the castle.<ref name="The Convert" /> 

Kryze continued evading enemy fire while Djarin jumped from the ship's lower bay to reach the castle's landing platform to get his [[N-1 starfighter]] for additional firepower. As one of the [[TIE series|TIE]] [[interceptor]]s fired on the landing platform in an attempt to destroy the N-1 starfighter, Djarin managed to power up his ship and get airborne. With the aid of Djarin's starfighter, the pair engaged and destroyed all six TIE interceptors pursuing them. Despite that, three [[TIE/sa tactical bomber|TIE/sa bombers]] arrived soon after and bombed the castle. Enraged, Kryze attempted to destroy all three [[bomber]]s. However, Kryze could only destroy one TIE bomber before reinforcements in the form of TIE interceptors arrived. Forced to flee, Djarin, including Kryze left the planet and jumped into [[hyperspace]]. They later arrived on a [[Armorer's planet|planet]] where the Children of the Watch were [[Mandalorian secret covert|based]].<ref name="The Convert" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:KryzeCastleConceptArt.png|thumb|right|350px|Ryan Church's concept art of Kryze Castle for ''The Mandalorian'' Season 3 "Chapter 17: The Apostate" episode]]
Kryze Castle was first revealed in the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Znsa4Deavgg trailer] for [[The Mandalorian Season Three|''The Mandalorian'' Season Three]] on [[January 16]], [[2023]].<ref name="The Mandalorian Season 3">{{SWYouTube|Znsa4Deavgg|The Mandalorian &#124; Season 3 Official Trailer &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/the-mandalorian-season-3-official-trailer}}</ref> It later made its first appearance in "[[Chapter 17: The Apostate]]" of the television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Apostate" /> which aired on [[Disney+]] on [[March 1]], 2023.<ref name="D23 March">{{D23|url=everything-new-you-can-stream-on-disney-in-march-2023|text=Everything New You Can Stream on Disney+ in March 2023}}</ref> The castle was first identified as Kryze Castle in the audio description for "[[Chapter 19: The Convert]]" episode<ref name="Audio Description" /> that released on Disney+ on [[March 15]], 2023.<ref name="D23 March" /> However, the capitalization of Kryze Castle is conjectural.<ref name="Audio Description" /> It was later identified as Kryze Fortress.<ref name="CGttSWG" /> The location of the castle was filmed at [[Wikipedia:Neist Point|Neist Point]] on the [[Wikipedia:Isle of Skye|Isle of Skye]], [[Wikipedia:Scotland|Scotland]].<ref name="Apostate" /><ref name="Neist Point Lighthoose">{{WebCite|url=https://www.photoawards.com/winner/zoom.php?eid=8-214136-21|text=Neist Point Lighthouse|author=David Nomdedeu|work=International Photography Awards|archivedate=20240524074953}}</ref>

Artists [[Ryan Church]] and [[Brett Northcutt]] created concept art of the exterior and the throne room of the castle. Concept art of Kryze sitting on the throne in the castle was done by artist [[Seth Engstrom]]. In one set of concept art by Northcutt, the throne room inside the castle had no vases. In another set of concept art by Engstrom, Kryze is depicted as sitting on a throne with animal [[Hair|fur]] and a piece of [[clothing]]. The cushions on the throne were depicted as having a navy [[Color|blue]], light green, and dark brown&ndash;like pattern.<ref name="MandoDowload The Apostate">{{SW|url=news/mando-download-chapter-17-the-apostate|text=Mando Download: "Chapter 17: The Apostate"}}</ref> One set of concept art by Northcutt showed Kryze at a viewing deck overlooking the sea.<ref name="MandoDowload The Mines of Mandalore">{{SW|url=news/mando-download-chapter-18-the-mines-of-mandalore|text=Mando Download: "Chapter 18: The Mines of Mandalore"}}</ref> One of the pictures created by Church showed two ''Kom'rk''-class fighters on the right and left-hand side of the castle.<ref name="MandoDownload The Convert">{{SW|url=news/mando-download-chapter-19-the-convert|text=Mando Download: "Chapter 19: The Convert"}}</ref>

